\###**19.6.3 Combining the data.frame** Next, use the code chunk below to add the statistics on the table.



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
spark <- report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarize('Monthly Sales' = list(Sales), 
            .groups = "drop")

sales <- report %>% 
  group_by(Product) %>% 
  summarise("Min" = min(Sales, na.rm = T),
            "Max" = max(Sales, na.rm = T),
            "Average" = mean(Sales, na.rm = T)
            )

sales_data = left_join(sales, spark)
```
:::



\###**19.6.4 Plotting the updated data.table**



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
sales_data %>%
  gt() %>%
  gt_plt_sparkline('Monthly Sales',
                   same_limit = FALSE)
